//:: cases TC_PST_25_RequiresNonHeapConflictsEnsuresFnUnsat
//:: tools silicon
//:: verdict Fail

// TC-PST-25: foo's non-heap precondition `n > 0` conflicts with its postcondition
// `isNeg(n)` (body: n < 0). isNeg has no precondition — its axiom fires unconditionally.
// Without supervisor's fix: postSat checks `inhale n < 0; assert false` — n < 0 is
// satisfiable in isolation (e.g. n = -1) → assert false fails → postUnsatisfiable does NOT fire (wrong).
// With supervisor's fix: postSat adds `n > 0` from foo's own precondition, making the
// check `inhale n > 0; inhale n < 0; assert false` — infeasible → postUnsatisfiable fires.

pure boolean isNeg(int n) = n < 0;

requires n > 0;
ensures isNeg(n);
void foo(int n) {
    assume false;  // makes normal verification vacuous; only postUnsatisfiable fires
}
